STM32F446 Logic Analyzer — KiCad Design Specification V1.0
Design baseline
This is your reference for designing the complete PCB in KiCad. It covers the component selection, footprints, electrical connections, power supply, CAN interface, signal capture and PCB design rules.

The goal is a minimal, professionally designed, USB-powered logic analyzer, using standard KiCad libraries, with no custom symbols or footprints.
1. Hardware specifications
Parameter	Design target
MCU	STM32F446RET6
Core	Cortex-M4, up to 180 MHz
Flash / SRAM	512 KB / 128 KB + 4 KB CCM
Digital channels	6 (D0–D5)
CAN	1 classical CAN interface (CAN-H/CAN-L)
Logic voltage	3.3 V only
USB	USB 2.0 Full Speed
Power	5 V from USB
Internal supply	3.3 V LDO
Programming	External ST-LINK using SWD
Capture	Timer-controlled sampling; DMA to be validated
Software	STM32 firmware + PyQt PC application
PCB	Four-layer FR-4, 1.6 mm
Assembly	IPC Class 2 target
Estimated board size	70 × 50 mm, preliminary

Important: CAN-H and CAN-L are two physical bus connections, not two independent sampled GPIO channels. Your board will provide six sampled GPIO channels and one decoded CAN bus.

The STM32F446RE is confirmed by ST's documentation, and its matching KiCad symbol is in the published standard libraries. 
