Final design recommendation: Keep revision A as a six-channel 3.3 V logic analyzer with passive CAN, USB Full Speed and SWD. It is a manageable project for learning PCB design, embedded firmware, hardware debugging and host-side protocol analysis without introducing unnecessary complexity.

The first schematic sheet to complete is MCU_Core, because it establishes the power pins, clock, reset and programming connections that every other sheet depends on.
